# Z (hand-back, last card step): the node agent is started. The agent loads its placement only after the platform's release step creates the serving container, so Z waits for it (up to 30 minutes)
# and the OPERATOR runs the release step during that wait with the owner's admin key; the key is never in a script. Z READS PASS when its log has 'node agent after start: active', whether the run
# ended green or timed out waiting for the container. Before it: prefix-reuse.off and levern.off must be ABSENT on the hub mount (the workflow refuses to start a gate or smoke job while one exists).
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the W-2 window pack (tp4-w2-levern-jobs: Lever N robustness, then the cutover; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/stage1-windows and push the job's tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Names no rig, card, host or registry. ORDER.txt has the order,
# the classes, the minutes, the boxes, the tags and every rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11 is the window image (the combined branch's engine with the Lever N traffic profile baked in as its
# default); a job that names tp4-serve-10 runs the production base image. C2_BOX_MINUTES is the job's box: the workflow enforces it from inside, it never cancels a run.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status agentstart
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11
